WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.512
For the hands-on work in this module we use five
small synthetic

00:00:03.538 --> 00:00:08.038
tables Keeping the datasets small makes it easier to
connect the SQL

00:00:08.062 --> 00:00:12.675
with the result you see on screen The admissions
table contains healthcare-style

00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:18.012
records such as patients diagnoses admission times
and discharge times We will

00:00:18.038 --> 00:00:23.675
use it for counts length-of-stay calculations and
conditional diagnosis metrics The

00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:29.388
sales table contains products quantities prices
categories and dates This table

00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:34.062
is useful for totals averages revenue calculations
WHERE and HAVING and running

00:00:34.088 --> 00:00:39.988
totals The employees table includes employee names
salaries departments and hire dates

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.075
We will use it when introducing window functions
such as ranking and

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:50.450
department averages The product_sales table is
intentionally compact It

00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:54.238
is designed to make ROLLUP CUBE GROUPING SETS and
GROUPING easier to

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:59.788
see Finally the grades table contains student course
grade and semester

00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:04.425
information It becomes part of the assignment
exercises near the end of

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:10.075
the module Everything is synthetic and disposable
The database runs

00:01:10.088 --> 00:01:13.625
in the browser and can be reset That makes it a safe

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:17.788
learning environment but still avoid pasting
sensitive or production data into a

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.562
teaching tool
